# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually copies: package
# manifests, tsconfigs and src. Everything below is either rebuilt inside the
# image or must never enter it.
#
# `.pglite-data` is the one that matters most: it is the LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# DATABASE — real rows, real phone numbers, real password hashes. Without this
# file it is uploaded to the daemon on every build and baked into the layer.

node_modules
dist
.pglite-data

# Local secrets. The Dockerfile never copies these; compose injects env at run
# time. Listing them means a stray file can't be picked up by a future COPY.
.env
.env.*

# Test and tooling files — `tsconfig.build.json` already excludes them from the
# compiled output, so shipping them only slows the context upload.
test
vitest.config.ts
drizzle.config.ts

# Deployment descriptors describe the image; they are not part of it.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile
backup

*.md
*.log
